# RECEIVED-VALUE-NOT-AN-EXPRESSION (steps/defects.md), in a method: x is the
# activation's own field, so no hidden-input boundary is involved; `x: 1 2` is
# still two values, refused at the extra one before native and walker split.
fn: m () int
    int: x 1
    x: 1 2
    return: x
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
